{"tool": "gh", "argv": ["pr", "create", "--base", "fh/7-submit-order", "--head", "fh/8-large-order-discount", "--title", "Add the large-order discount (8)", "--body", "After the volume and tier discounts, an order whose remaining amount is at least `LARGE_ORDER_THRESHOLD` (500.00) gets `LARGE_ORDER_PERCENT` (2) off, before any coupon; both in orders/config.py. `quote` lists it as `large-order`; it is spread over the lines and taxed like the other order-level discounts. `report daily` lists it as `large-order` and never as coupon: orders without a coupon attribute the whole rest after volume and tier to it, coupon orders use the stored coupon to find the split that adds up to the stored total (orders placed before this change keep their full coupon amount). A coupon's minimum is still checked before this discount. Engine, report and CLI tests.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)"], "cwd": "/private/var/folders/fd/j548rpgd0bz5n99xbntzf0100000gn/T/fh-eta-validate-r2/p3-orders-opus/repo"}
